#!/usr/bin/python3
"""1337: a session runner for 1337 workstations.

$HOME is small and follows you between workstations; /goinfre is large but
belongs to one machine and is wiped. Everything this runner does is described
in ~/1337.yml: the folders to move out of $HOME, the tools to install, the
repos to clone at login and push at logout, and the order of every step.
`1337 setup` writes that file from 1337.example.yml and your answers; the rest
of this file only knows how to read it and carry it out.
"""

